access_tokenid: answer foreign ioctls (terminal probes) with ENOTTY and without a log line. Services and apps
call isatty()/TIOCGWINSZ (ioctl type 'T', 84) on their /dev/access_token_id descriptor many times a second (in
one 10-minute kernel log of the phone: 1761 of 4465 messages, from OH's time_service and telephony_sa among
others). Each was logged at error level ("access tokenid magic fail, TYPE=84"): at a console loglevel above 1
the flood, drawn on the framebuffer console, froze the phone; at loglevel=1 it still fills the printk ring, which
then covers only minutes before a hang. ENOTTY is what a file that is not a terminal answers.

diff --git a/drivers/accesstokenid/access_tokenid.c b/drivers/accesstokenid/access_tokenid.c
index a9340d471..b19b522fe 100644
--- a/drivers/accesstokenid/access_tokenid.c
+++ b/drivers/accesstokenid/access_tokenid.c
@@ -338,9 +338,15 @@ static long access_tokenid_ioctl(struct file *file, unsigned int cmd,
 	}
 
 	if (_IOC_TYPE(cmd) != ACCESS_TOKEN_ID_IOCTL_BASE) {
-		pr_err("%s: access tokenid magic fail, TYPE=%d\n",
-		       __func__, _IOC_TYPE(cmd));
-		return -EINVAL;
+		/*
+		 * Not one of ours: typically a terminal probe (isatty(),
+		 * TIOCGWINSZ) on this descriptor, which some services and
+		 * app SDKs issue many times a second. Answer as a file that
+		 * is not a terminal does, without filling the kernel log.
+		 */
+		pr_debug_ratelimited("%s: ioctl type %d is not ours\n",
+				     __func__, _IOC_TYPE(cmd));
+		return -ENOTTY;
 	}
 
 	if (func_cmd >= ACCESS_TOKENID_MAX_NR) {
